{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"minimumCut","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"capacity","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cut","identifier":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/Cut","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Flows3CutV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedView","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdditiveArithmetic","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Comparable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The cut minimizes the capacity of the edges between a nonempty proper vertex set and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rest. The side holding the first vertex is the source side. Computed by Nagamochi–Ibaraki:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"maximum adjacency orderings that contract every edge whose scanned connection is at least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the best cut so far. Which minimum cut is returned when several exist is unspecified, but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the same input always gives the same cut.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the result is the cut of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel capacities add and self-loops are ignored. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"capacity"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge, in position order, before any work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sums are formed in a wider type than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":" where needed ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int128"},{"type":"text","text":" for fixed-width"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integers, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Float"},{"type":"text","text":"), so a contracted group’s connection may exceed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"C"},{"type":"text","text":"’s range."}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Complexity","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(nm log n) in the worst case."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"type":"aside","name":"Precondition","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every capacity is at least zero, not NaN and finite, and the minimum cut’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value fits in ","type":"text"},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (it is at most every vertex’s capacity sum).","type":"text"}]}]}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumCut(capacity:)"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Flows\/documentation\/Flows\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A global minimum cut over ","type":"text"},{"code":"directedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or nil below two vertices.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","title":"minimumCut(capacity:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumCut"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"capacity"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:5Flows3CutV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Cut"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols12DirectedViewV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"C","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"externalID":"s:14G